  "verbalization": "Dexamethasone is linked to X-linked Adrenal Hypoplasia Congenita through a chain of indications that ultimately point to Methylprednisolone, a corticosteroid with similar pharmacological properties. The evidence suggests that Dexamethasone may be used in conditions where Methylprednisolone is prescribed, and in turn, Methylprednisolone is associated with X-linked Adrenal Hypoplasia Congenita. This relationship is supported by the shared use of Methylprednisolone in multiple conditions, including Chronic Beryllium Disease and Erythema Multiforme, which are both linked to X-linked Adrenal Hypoplasia Congenita. The presence of a common pathway involving Methylprednisolone implies a potential mechanistic link, though the exact nature of this relationship remains unclear. The evidence highlights a possible dependency on corticosteroids in the development of this condition, but further research is needed to establish a definitive causal or functional connection.",
